§§ DESIGN-PILLARS
  a model-install via scripts/m2_install_models.sh
  b real-backend execution : 3 models × 7 files = 21 measurements
  c per-token NLL recorded + visualized
  d bootstrap-CI computed (1000 resamples)
  e paraphrase-quality scores checked + flagged
  f Apocky-review interface for paraphrases
  g stratified-target validation per-mode
  h audit-chain populates with-real-runs
  i comparison-harness re-run with-real-models
  j HTML-report auto-generated + committed to eval/m2_results/

§§ TASK BREAKDOWN

  P1.1 : MODEL INSTALL + VERIFY ~2 hours wallclock
    bash scripts/m2_install_models.sh
    ∀ 3 models : download + SHA-256 verify
    disk-budget verify ≤ 8GB total
    llama.cpp subprocess-smoke-test per-model
    deliverables :
      ~/.cslv3-m2-models/ populated + verified
      scripts/m2_install_models.log
    acceptance :
      ✓ 3/3 models installed + SHA-match
      ✓ llama.cpp smoke-query returns valid-logits per-model

  P1.2 : PARAPHRASE APOCKY-REVIEW ~30 min Apocky-time
    generate m2_quality scores for-all-7 paraphrases
    flag any with-cosine < 0.7 OR entity-recall < 0.8
    present to Apocky with quality-scores + diff-view
    Apocky-edits OR approves each
    deliverables :
      eval/paraphrases/*.en ← Apocky-reviewed final
      eval/paraphrases/review_log.md ← change-log
    acceptance :
      ✓ 7/7 paraphrases Apocky-approved
      ✓ ∀ quality-score ≥ threshold OR override-documented

  P1.3 : REAL-BACKEND FULL RUN ~30-60 min wallclock
    python scripts/compute_m2.py --all-eval --bootstrap=1000
    capture : per-(file × model) m₂ + CI-low + CI-high
    capture : per-token NLL arrays
    emit audit-chain entries for all 21 runs
    deliverables :
      eval/m2_baseline.json ← real-data (replaces mock)
      eval/m2_results/real_run_<timestamp>/ ← per-run HTML reports
      .m2-chain/runs.jsonl ← +21 real entries
      .m2-cache/ populated
    acceptance :
      ✓ 21/21 measurements completed (no model-timeout)
      ✓ bootstrap-CI computed for all-21
      ✓ audit-chain verify-clean
      ✓ visualization-reports committed
      ✓ per-token NLL arrays captured

  P1.4 : STRATIFIED-TARGET VALIDATION
    evaluate m₂ per-mode against Session-11 stratified-targets
      pure-CSL  ≤ 1.5
      bridge    ≤ 1.2
      prose     ≤ 1.05
    per-model agreement : flag high-variance-across-models (>20% spread)
    deliverables :
      eval/m2_stratified_report.md
      diag/M2_INTERPRETATION.md updated with-real-numbers
    acceptance :
      ✓ ∀ stratified-targets met OR documented-deviation-with-rationale
      ✓ multi-model agreement within-20% per-file OR flagged
      ✓ interpretation-doc updated

  P1.5 : COMPARISON-HARNESS REAL RUN
    python scripts/m2_compare.py --notations=csl,apl,lojban,prose
    5 algorithm-reference passages × 4 notations × 3 models = 60 measurements
    deliverables :
      benchmarks/m2_comparison.md ← real-data
      eval/m2_results/comparison_real/ ← HTML
    acceptance :
      ✓ 60/60 measurements completed
      ✓ comparison-table shows CSL density-position quantitatively
      ✓ caveats-documented (APL/Lojban LLM-unfamiliarity)

  P1.6 : v1.1.0 PROMOTION ← after-P1.1-.5 green
    update VERSION : 1.1.0 (drop -rc.1)
    update CHANGELOG : consolidate rc.1 + real-data entries into 1.1.0
    update STABILITY.md : T25 marked stable
    tag : git tag -a v1.1.0 -m "Release v1.1.0 — T25 m₂ with real-backend validation"
    release.cmd → rebuild dist/ @ 1.1.0
    deliverables :
      dist/cslv3-1.1.0-windows-x64/ bundle
      git tag v1.1.0 pushed
      CHANGELOG 1.1.0 entry finalized
    acceptance :
      ✓ all-17-Session-10 gates green
      ✓ all-2-T25-gates green (mock + real)
      ✓ release-script clean
      ✓ manifest signed

