    ✓ SESSION_4_HANDOFF.csl + all-subsequent round-trip clean
    ✓ existing-parse ¬ regressed (all-prior-gates green)
    ✓ prose-context explicit-opt-in (¬ auto-promote)
    ✓ documented in specs/13_GRAMMAR_SELF.csl §§ prose-context-extension

§§ P2.3 : WORKSPACE-INDEX SQLITE PERSISTENCE
  current : LSP workspace_index.rs rebuilds in-memory per-session
  goal : persist across-session via SQLite
  scope : additive-LSP-internal (no-protocol-change)
  files-modified :
    lsp/server/src/workspace_index.rs : SQLite backing
    lsp/server/Cargo.toml : rusqlite already-present (verify)
    lsp/server/tests/integration.rs : +persistence-test
  schema :
    files(uri TEXT PRIMARY KEY, mtime INTEGER, content_hash TEXT)
    symbols(file_uri TEXT, name TEXT, kind TEXT, line INTEGER, col INTEGER, type_info TEXT)
    FOREIGN KEY symbols(file_uri) REFERENCES files(uri)
  cache-dir : ~/.cslv3-lsp-cache/<workspace-hash>/index.sqlite
  acceptance :
    ✓ cold-start workspace-reload ≤ 100ms (after-first-build)
    ✓ mtime-check invalidates-stale entries
    ✓ cross-session symbol-lookup works
    ✓ SQLite file-size bounded (<50MB typical)

§§ P2.4 : RANGE-FORMATTING AST-SUBTREE
  current : range-formatting falls-back to full-file
  goal : extract AST-subtree in-range + pprint-subtree + splice
  files-modified :
    lsp/server/src/formatting.rs : range-subtree extraction
    parser/main.odin : --range-fmt=L1,C1,L2,C2 subcommand (additive)
    parser/pprint.odin : subtree-pprint entry-point (additive)
  acceptance :
    ✓ range-format preserves-surroundings byte-exact
    ✓ partial-node ranges expanded-to-smallest-containing-node
    ✓ multi-selection ranges supported
    ✓ latency ≤ 50ms for small-ranges

═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§ PHASE-3 : P4 FINE-TUNE EXPERIMENT ← alternate density-validation
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  W! research-grade • shows LLMs CAN-learn density-notation
  ≡ m₂ measures distance-from-base • P4 measures reducible-gap

§§ DESIGN-PILLARS
  a pick smallest model from P1 (1B param)
  b fine-tune on CSL-corpus (specs/ + tests/ + examples/)
  c measure m₂-post-tune vs m₂-pre-tune
  d hypothesis : m₂-post ≪ m₂-pre ← density-claim confirmed-differently
  e reproducibility : LoRA weights committed OR training-script pinned

§§ TRAINING SETUP
  method : LoRA fine-tuning (parameter-efficient)
    ∵ full-finetune infeasible on-dev-hw
    ∵ LoRA 8-16 rank sufficient for-notation-adaptation
  tools :
    llama.cpp + llama-finetune-lora OR
    unsloth (if-available + CPU-compatible)
    OR axolotl (requires GPU ← fallback-only)
  training-data :
    sources : specs/*.csl + tests/*.csl + examples/*.csl + eval/*.csl
    estimate : ~50KB CSL-text corpus
    format : next-token-prediction on raw-CSL
    held-out : 20% of corpus for-validation-NLL
  hyper-parameters :
    rank : 8 (minimal)
    lr : 1e-4
    epochs : 3-5
    batch-size : 1 (CPU)
  budget : ≤ 12 hours wallclock on-dev-hw
  if-GPU-available : ≤ 2 hours

§§ FILES-NEW
  scripts/m2_finetune.py             ~400-LOC training-driver
  scripts/m2_measure_posttune.py     ~200-LOC post-measurement
  training_data/                     corpus-for-tuning
    train.jsonl   ~80% of CSL-corpus
    valid.jsonl   ~20% held-out
  artifacts/lora_weights/            trained-adapter (if-committed)
  artifacts/finetune_log.md          loss-curves + metrics
  eval/m2_posttune_results/          HTML reports
  diag/M2_FINETUNE_INTERPRETATION.md
  tests/test_m2_finetune.py ~150-LOC smoke-test

§§ MEASUREMENTS
  pre-tune m₂ : from P1.3 real-backend run
  post-tune m₂ : same 7 files × same model (now-fine-tuned)
  expected : m₂-post-tune approaches-1.0 (density-claim confirmed-learnable)
  reported : delta-m₂ per-file
  also-reported : validation-NLL curves during-training
  caveat : overfitting risk ← held-out set must-show-improvement

§§ ACCEPTANCE
  ✓ fine-tune completes on-dev-hw within-budget
  ✓ training-loss curves recorded + smooth-convergence
  ✓ validation-NLL improves-or-stable (no-overfit-catastrophe)
  ✓ m₂-post-tune measured + compared to-pre-tune
  ✓ delta-m₂ reported per-file with-interpretation
  ✓ LoRA weights committed OR training-script fully-reproducible

